2 Diversify your investments seven or eight ways;
you don’t know what risks lie ahead.
3 Heavy clouds drop rain;
a tree stays where it falls.
4 If you keep worrying about the weather, you won’t sow;
if you keep watching the clouds, you won’t reap.
5 Just like you don’t know where the wind will blow
or how bones form in a womb, you don’t understand what God’s doing who makes everything happen.
6 Plant your seed in the morning;
don’t be idle in the afternoon;
you don’t know if planting in the morning or afternoon is best, or if one’s as good as the other. Eccl 11:1-6
7 Light is pleasing; sunrise is pleasant to behold.
8 If you live a long time, enjoy all your years; just remember, there’ll be lots of dark days, and nothing will seem important in the end.
9 Young people, enjoy life while you’re young; stay pleasant. Go ahead and follow your impulses and desires; just remember, God will judge you for all of them. 10So don’t worry; take care of your health, because childhood and the prime of life soon pass. Eccl 11:7-10

