Psalms Chapter 38 A Psalm of David
for a Memorial
1 Yahveh, don’t rebuke me in your wrath
or discipline me in your furious anger.
2 Your arrows have pierced deep into me;
your hand has come down hard on me.
3 Because of your indignation, my body’s not sound;
by my sin I’ve ruined my health.
4 My iniquities have piled up higher than my head
and weighed me down.
5 My wounds have festered and grown foul. My foolish choices 6 have doubled me over;
I grieve all the time;
7I’m burning up with fever;
my health is broken.
8I’m numb and crushed,
and groan from inner conflict. Ps 38:1-8
9 Yahveh, you know what I long for;
you hear my sighs.
10 My heart’s pounding, my strength’s failing;
the sparkle in my eyes is gone.
11 My friends and loved ones stand back from my sickness;
my relatives stay well away from me.
12 Those who want to kill me lay snares for me;
the ones that want to injure me threaten destruction,
constantly plotting treachery. Ps 38:9-12
13 But like someone deaf, I don’t hear;
like a mute I don’t speak.
14 Yes, I’m like somebody that can’t hear,
someone with no arguments to offer.
15 I’m depending on you, Yahveh;
you’ll have to answer for me:
16 Don’t let them celebrate over me
or gloat when my foot slips.
17 I’m ready to fall;
my sorrow continually looms in front of me.
18 I’m confessing my iniquity; I’m anxious about my sin.
19 But my enemies are vigorous and strong;
they hate me for no reason.
20and repay bad for good because I follow after what’s good.
21 Don’t leave me, Yahveh; stay close by!
22 Hurry and help me, Lord my savior! Ps 38:13-22

Psalms Chapter 40 For the Choir Director. A Psalm of David
1 I waited patiently for the LORD;
he listened to my call for help.
2 He brought me up out of the pit of despair, out of the muddy clay,
set my feet on solid rock,
and made my footsteps secure.
3 He put a new song in me, a song about praising God;
other people will hear it, see what he’s done, and trust in him. 4 How blessed people are that trust in the LORD
instead of turning to proud or deceitful people.
5 LORD my God, you’ve done so many amazing things;
your good intentions for us are too many to tell.
Nobody compares with you;
if I tried to tell about your wonderful acts,
I couldn’t recount them all.
Ps 40:1-5
6 Your don’t delight in sacrifices and meal offerings;
you haven’t required burnt offerings and sin offerings;
you’ve pierced my ears [Heb 10:5-8a, 9a; “you gave me a body”LXX.]
7 Then I said, “I’m coming;
it’s written about me in the scroll;
8I delight in doing your will, my God;
I have your Law at heart.”
9 In the great assembly
I’ve proclaimed the good news about goodness
I didn’t hold back
10 or keep to myself the truth about your goodness;
I spoke openly about your saving power,
about your enduring love and truth. Ps 40:6-10
11 LORD, don’t withhold your mercy from me;
let your enduring love and truth keep protecting me.
12 Troubles beyond number surround me,
and my own sins overtake me till I can’t see any way to escape them.
13 LORD, please hurry and help me.
14 Embarrass and humiliate those who keep trying to destroy me;
disgrace the ones that delight in hurting me.
15 Make them appalled at their disgrace
who say to me, “Aha, aha!”
16 Make them happy who look to you, who love your salvation and chant, “The LORD is great.”
17 Keep me in your thoughts because I’m in misery and need you,
my helper, my deliverer.
Don’t delay.
Ps 40:11-17

