A. The process of hermeneutics and life [understanding the biblical message]
&amp;nbsp;
1. Goal: to find out what the scripture means by experiencing what it says; do it to understand it.
&amp;nbsp;
Passages take on a liveliness and relevance because of experiences we face. Meaning is not just objective significance, but subjective impact. The two correspond as to content, but the impact comes from the doing. Understanding through interpretation …

Psalms Chapter 51 Psalm for the Choir Director. A Psalm of David,
When Nathan the Prophet Came to Him, After He’d Slept with Bathsheba
1 Be gracious to me, God, in proportion to your enduring love;
according to your great mercy, blot out my transgressions.
2 Wash me thoroughly from my sin;
cleanse me from my iniquity.
3 I know my failings;
my sin always weighs on my mind.
4 I’ve sinned against you and you only; I did what you consider evil;
so you’re justified in what you say to me,
blameless when you condemn me [Rom 3:4].
Ps 51:1-4
5 I was born in sin;
in iniquity my mother conceived me.
6 You want truth in the inward self;
you’ll make me know wisdom in myself.
7 Purify me with hyssop, and I’ll be clean;
wash me, and I’ll be whiter than snow.
8 Fill me with joy and happiness again,
and let the bones you broke mend up.
9 Don’t look at my sins;
blot out my iniquities.
Ps 51:5-9
10 Create a clean heart in me, God;
renew a steadfast spirit within me.
11 Don’t banish me from your presence
or take your Holy Spirit away from me.
12 Restore to me the joy your salvation brings;
grant me a willing attitude to obey.
13 Then I’ll teach transgressors your ways;
sinners will be converted to you.
14 Deliver me from being guilty of murder
so I can joyfully sing about your goodness.
15 LORD, open my lips
so I can express your praises.
16 You don’t delight in sacrifice; otherwise, I’d give it;
you’re not pleased with burnt offerings.
17The sacrifice you want is a broken spirit;
you appreciate a repentant heart.
18 In your good favor, do good to Zion;
build up the walls around Jerusalem.
19 Then you’ll delight in godly sacrifices,
in burnt offerings and whole burnt offerings;
then young bulls will again be offered on your altar.
Ps 51:10-19

